<title>UK: Plantation shares spike on takeover talk.</title>
<headline>Plantation shares spike on takeover talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Plantation and General Investments Plc leapt over 20 percent on Tuesday after news of a possible takeover offer by Rovida International Ltd.</p>
<p>Plantation and General shares were up 11p at 63-1/2p at 1423 GMT.</p>
<p>In a statement to the market Rovida said it was in the early stages of considering a possible offer for the company.</p>
<p>Such an offer would be be in the region of 58p cash per ordinary Plantation and General share, and would be subject to major shareholder approval.</p>
<p>Simon Gardner, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
